WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.440
Avengers: Endgame was the epic culmination
of over 20 movies released across more than

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:09.800
a decade, earning well over two billion dollars
at the global box office.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.380
So why would Disney re-release the movie less
than two months after its debut?

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.860
Here are a few reasons.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.280
One big reason why Endgame is getting another
push in theaters doesn't have anything to

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.740
do with the Avengers at all.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:25.880
It's another blockbuster that still holds
the top spot at the global box office.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:27.260
"Tell me his name again."

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:33.160
In 2009, James Cameron's Avatar brought in
more than $2.7 billion, easily claiming the

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.920
all-time box office crown with its 3-D, sci-fi
spectacle.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.940
It's held on to the record for an entire decade,
but that era may be about to meet its end.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.899
The Avengers made a major splash with a record-setting
opening, with Endgame becoming the fastest

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.320
film to ever surpass $2 billion.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:53.940
It eclipsed the entire box office revenue
of its predecessor, Infinity War, in just

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.380
11 days.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:59.100
But the new movie soon began getting pushed
out of theaters by an onslaught of summer

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:04.040
blockbusters, leaving it around $43 million
shy of the all-time record after two months

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.020
in theaters.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:09.040
In hyping up a new release of the movie, it's
clear that Marvel is in it to win it, and

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.380
this scheme might be just the thing to push
the MCU over James Cameron's otherworldly

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.380
odyssey.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.780
The fourth Avengers movie already tops out
at a stunning three-hour runtime, and the

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.020
re-release will apparently be even more demanding
of the audience.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.100
But don't go in expecting the full director's
cut treatment.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:29.619
According to Marvel Studios president Kevin
Feige, the movie's not going to include new

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:32.000
scenes, at least not before the credits.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.460
Speaking to Screen Rant, the super-producer
explained that the Endgame re-release is,

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:48.320
Rather than being a re-edited version of the
film, Feige implied that the re-release is

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.820
more of a, quote, "bit of a marketing push,
with a few new things at the end of the movie."

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.880
But what could those new things be?

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:59.499
We don't know, but here are some possibilities:
The re-release could include a deleted scene

00:01:59.499 --> 00:02:04.289
featuring 13 Reasons Why's Katherine Langford
as Tony's grown-up daughter, encountering

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:07.040
him in the orange "Soul World" after Tony's
snap.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.780
According to directors Joe and Anthony Russo,
that scene was deleted for being too out-there

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:13.820
of a story turn at a critical moment.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:17.140
As Joe Russo told the Happy Sad Confused podcast,

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:35.540
There's also a possibility that this package
might include a previously-unreleased sequence

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:40.860
of Luis from the Ant-Man movies recapping
the entire MCU, which Kevin Feige confirmed

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.180
the existence of during a Reddit "Ask Me Anything"
thread in May.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.380
According to Feige,

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.100
And those are just the possibilities we know
about.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:02.480
The real answer is, nobody knows what Marvel
has planned for the re-release package, but

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:06.660
based on Feige's description, it's probably
best to temper your expectations.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:11.280
The re-release announcement was even more
surprising considering that Endgame will return

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.980
to theaters shortly before the July 2nd release
of the next Spider-Man film, Far from Home.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:20.040
But it could actually turn out to be a big
boost for Tom Holland's next outing as New

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.140
York's friendly neighborhood webslinger.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:26.840
This won't be the first time Marvel has debuted
a new movie against one of its biggest performers.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:32.120
In early 2018, Black Panther and Infinity
War ended up running concurrently in theaters,

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:36.300
and both films performed massively well at
the box office without stepping on each other's

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:37.240
toes.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:41.400
And as far as Endgame goes, this won't even
be the first time it's running against another

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.600
one of Marvel's own.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.580
Captain Marvel, which was released over a
month before Endgame, saw a small bump in

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:50.180
ticket sales once it was joined in theaters
by the juggernaut sequel.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:56.520
More than any other MCU movie since…ever,
Endgame feels like a real conclusion, wrapping

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.580
up a story that's spanned some fans' whole
childhoods.

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:04.060
With both Iron Man and Captain America apparently
out of the roster, it might be tempting for

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:06.240
some viewers to want to jump off the train.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.280
But while one chapter of the MCU may be ending,
it's clear that Marvel isn't ready to bow

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.200
out of the pop culture spotlight.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:16.720
Re-releasing Endgame puts the movie back in
the news for the summer season, making headlines

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:21.640
all over the internet, getting audiences ready
for the final phase 3 movie and beyond.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:26.160
It also keeps the brand name in the news cycle
during the run-up to July's San Diego Comic-Con

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:31.680
and Disney's D23 Expo in August, at which
the company is expected to roll out big announcements

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:33.080
for its upcoming films.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:37.060
So if you're still wondering when the superhero
bubble is going to burst, you might want to

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:39.620
get used to the possibility that it never
will.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.440
"You see?

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:42.820
No one's going anywhere."

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:47.171
While some fans were enthused by the news
of Endgame's theatrical victory lap, it's

00:04:47.171 --> 00:04:51.570
hard not to have a cynical view of the announcement,
especially with Feige himself calling the

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:54.600
re-release more of a marketing thing than
anything else.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:59.400
After all, just a few days before the announcement,
Anthony Russo told Indiewire that he wasn't

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.820
focusing on the box office battle between
Endgame and Avatar.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:07.240
So it can't help but feel like less of an
artistic move than it is a money grab.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.040
But it might well be an effective one.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:13.340
One more weekend with enthusiastic Marvel
fans could be all it takes to close the gap

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.000
between Avengers and Avatar.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.540
But if that happens, who really wins?

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:23.460
After its high-profile merger with Fox, Disney
now owns not only Marvel, but Avatar as well.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:27.940
In other words, the company already has the
two highest-grossing movies of all time, they're

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:29.640
just pitting them against each other.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:31.620
"It's all going the same place."

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:36.460
Another, less obvious winner is actress Zoe
Saldana, who has a prominent role in both

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:37.600
franchises.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:43.180
She's blue, she's green, she's a billion-dollar
woman, and she's come a long way from Crossroads,

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:45.440
playing supporting act to Britney Spears.

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:48.260
"You're just jealous."

